    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"Edgecase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.layout_kamada_kawai - Edgecase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"Edgecase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.layout_kamada_kawai.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.layout_kamada_kawai()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | Edgecase\n  description: >-\n    Place the nodes so that drawn distances match shortest-path distances.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.layout_kamada_kawai()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | Edgecase\n  description: >-\n    Place the nodes so that drawn distances match shortest-path distances.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.layout_kamada_kawai()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: >-\n  Place the nodes so that drawn distances match shortest-path distances.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nPlace the nodes so that drawn distances match shortest-path distances.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L5922-L6040){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.layout_kamada_kawai(\n    weighted=None,\n    initial=None,\n    max_iter=500,\n    tol=1e-06,\n    scale=1.0,\n    center=(0.0, 0.0),\n    attr_name=None,\n    return_dict=False,\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Kamada-Kawai layout](../assets/graphs/layout-kamada-kawai.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"On the left, a three-by-three grid graph scattered at random. On the right, layout_kamada_kawai() sets the distance between every two nodes to match their number of hops, which straightens the grid into three rows of three.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nThe Kamada-Kawai layout treats every pair of nodes as joined by a spring whose rest\nlength is their shortest-path distance `d_ij`, and minimizes the total spring energy\n`sum (|x_i - x_j| - d_ij)^2 / d_ij^2`. The `1 / d_ij^2` factor makes nearby pairs\nmatter most, so local structure is drawn faithfully while far-apart pairs are allowed\nto bend. The result is centered and scaled so the largest coordinate is `scale=`.\n\nCompared with `layout_spring()` the layout is deterministic (it starts from a circle,\nnot random positions), edge lengths come out more uniform, and the global shape of\npaths, grids and trees is usually clearer. Each sweep costs `O(n^2)`, plus an\nall-pairs shortest-path computation up front, so it is best for graphs of up to a few\nthousand nodes.\n\nNetworkX's `kamada_kawai_layout()` minimizes the same energy with the L-BFGS\nquasi-Newton method. This method first runs stress majorization sweeps (Gansner,\nKoren & North, 2004), which move one node at a time to its best position and settle\nthe overall shape reliably, then finishes with L-BFGS, which is much faster through\nthe long, flat stretches of the energy (a path straightening out) where sweeps crawl.\nThe two reach the same kind of layout, though not always the same local minimum.\nDistances ignore edge direction.\nPairs in different components, which have no path, are given a distance one more than\nthe largest finite one (NetworkX uses a fixed `1e6`), so components sit near one\nanother rather than drifting apart.\n\nPositions are stored as `[x, y]` lists in the `attr_name=` node attribute; see\n`layout_circular()`.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[weighted]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[bool]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True`, edge weights (`1` where missing) are edge lengths for the shortest\n    paths, and parallel edges use their lightest weight. If `False`, every edge has\n    length `1`. If `None` (default), follows whether the graph was created as weighted.\n\n<code>[initial]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[Union[str, dict]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Starting positions, as the name of a node attribute holding `(x, y)` pairs or a\n    dict mapping node IDs or labels to pairs; nodes without one start on the circle.\n    If `None` (default), all nodes start evenly spaced on the unit circle, in ID order.\n\n<code>[max_iter]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[500]{.dv}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Maximum number of majorization sweeps, and separately of L-BFGS iterations.\n    Default is `500`.\n\n<code>[tol]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [float]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[1e-06]{.fl}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Stop once an L-BFGS iteration lowers the energy by at most this fraction. Default\n    is `1e-6`.\n\n<code>[scale]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[float]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[1.0]{.fl}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Largest coordinate after rescaling. `None` keeps the raw coordinates, in units of\n    edge length (`center=` is then ignored). Default is `1.0`.\n\n<code>[center]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [tuple[float, float]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [(0.0, 0.0)]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Center of the layout, as `(x, y)`. Default is the origin.\n\n<code>[attr_name]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Node attribute to store the positions in. If `None` (default), uses `\"pos\"`.\n\n<code>[return_dict]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[False]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True`, returns a dictionary instead of self. If `False` (default), stores the\n    positions on the nodes and returns self for chaining.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Union[dict[int, tuple[float, float]], Graph]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If `return_dict=` is `True`: dictionary mapping node IDs to `(x, y)` tuples. If\n    `return_dict=` is `False` (default): returns self for method chaining.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If `weighted=True` and an edge weight is not positive, `tol=` is negative, an\n    initial position is not a pair of finite numbers, or `scale=` or `center=` is\n    invalid.\n:::\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nWith `scale=None` the coordinates are in units of edge length, so the two ends of a\npath of five edges come out five apart:\n\n::: {#da4db43a .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\npos = ec.Graph().add_path_graph(6).layout_kamada_kawai(scale=None, return_dict=True)\nx1, y1 = pos[1]\nx6, y6 = pos[6]\nround(((x6 - x1) ** 2 + (y6 - y1) ** 2) ** 0.5, 3)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n5.0\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#6a056fce .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nec.football().layout_kamada_kawai().plot(layout=\"pos\", show_labels=False)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1em auto\">\n<style>.ec-plot > svg { display:block; max-width:100%; height:auto; }</style>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"700\" height=\"500\" viewBox=\"21.0 15.0 658.0 470.0\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;\">\n<rect x=\"21.0\" y=\"15.0\" width=\"658.0\" height=\"470.0\" fill=\"#fafafa\"/>\n<path d=\"M324.5,342.0 C326.3,334.9 335.2,312.1 335.3,299.6 C335.4,287.1 326.6,272.5 324.8,267.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"0.8999999999999999\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" data-edge=\"22-10-0\" data-attrs='{}'/>\n<line x1=\"328.2\" y1=\"343.5\" x2=\"356.2\" y2=\"294.1\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"0.8999999999999999\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" data-edge=\"22-12-1\" data-attrs='{}'/>\n<line x1=\"319.4\" y1=\"341.6\" x2=\"316.8\" y2=\"314.6\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"0.8999999999999999\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" data-edge=\"22-13-2\" data-attrs='{}'/>\n<path d=\"M325.0,342.2 C328.3,330.9 340.1,288.1 344.6,274.4 C349.2,260.8 350.8,262.7 352.1,260.3\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"0.8999999999999999\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" data-edge=\"22-18-3\" data-attrs='{}'/>\n<line x1=\"325.6\" y1=\"370.8\" x2=\"343.8\" y2=\"424.8\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"0.8999999999999999\" stroke-opacity=\"0.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round